#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE2253 expect=skipped domain=TT
#note "Plan B phase 4d (owner rulings Q2 / B-Q10): the rule now declares Requirements.Variables.Any [TTENRL, TTDUR]. NEITHER listed column is declared here, so the Any leg is unmet and the rule SKIPS instead of firing once per dataset. That is the deliberate semantic change the adoption exists for — the all-absent case is nothing-to-check, not a defect (M2-D24 / M3-F.1) — and it is why the violation pins that stood here are gone. This scenario is Gate C evidence for 4d: BOTH findings snapshots are structurally blind to it (te.json / te.xpt carry both columns; the SEND rules have no snapshot rows at all)."
#library standard=sendig version=dart-1-1
dataset TT class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Stages"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col RSTGCD  type=Char label="Repro Stage Code"
col RSTAGE  type=Char label="Description of Repro Stage"
col TTSTRL  type=Char label="Rule for Start of Repro Stage"
---
S1 | TT | PREMATE | Premating | Day 1
S1 | TT | GESTATE | Gestation | GD 0
